# Generated language code. Nothing here is committed; CI regenerates it.
gen/

# The exported proto trees the buffers CLI compiles against: copies of
# googleapis, protovalidate and the well-known types, written by
# scripts/export-protos.sh. Vendored dependencies, not output.
build/

# schema/ is NOT ignored. The .fbs and .capnp are the deliverable for a
# consumer who wants FlatBuffers or Cap'n Proto without installing buf, the
# buffers plugin and a protobuf toolchain first -- the same reason protobuf/
# is committed rather than generated on demand. CI regenerates and diffs them,
# so a committed file that drifts from the schema fails the build.
#
# The ordinal ledger buffers.lock is committed for a stronger reason: it is
# the record that field slots have not moved.

# Descriptor sets, built on demand by the lint and schema steps.
*.binpb
